			"date": "2023-02-25T14:25:45.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.social/@techytacos\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>techytacos</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@eleventy\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eleventy</span></a></span> What do you think causes the hampering of developer speed? Gazelle can automate much of the management of bazel build files. You could imagine getting to a place where you write your source files and bazel pretty much knows how to build them automatically.</p>",
